    "https://jobs.unisg.ch/offene-stellen/administration-und-organisation-des-lehrstuhlsekretariats-m-w-d/caf86dd9-ecf0-4fb9-bc90-817862f21e88": {
      "title": "HSG: Administration und Organisation des Lehrstuhlsekretariats (m/w/d)",
      "description": "HSG: Administration und Organisation des Lehrstuhlsekretariats (m/w/d) Institut für Produktions- und Supply Chain Management (PSCM-HSG) Administration und Organisation des Lehrstuhlsekretariats (m/w/d) Administration und Organisation des Lehrstuhlsekretariats (m/w/d) 50 %\n            \n            \n                ( ab\n                \n                    01.11.2026, unbefristet) Ihre Aufgaben Sekretariat & Kommunikation - Sie sind die zentrale Anlaufstelle für den Lehrstuhl und den Kernhaushalt und verantworten die Termin- und Reiseplanung für die Lehrstuhlinhaberin/den Lehrstuhlinhaber. Dabei pflegen Sie eine hochprofessionelle, verbindliche Kommunikation mit Lehrstuhlpartnern, Gremien und externen Kontakten und vertreten den Lehrstuhl nach aussen souverän in Wort und Schrift. Personaladministration - Sie betreuen die Spesenabrechnungen und Zeiterfassung für studentische Hilfskräfte und Mitarbeitende, begleiten Vertragserstellungen und den Bewerbungsprozess und unterstützen bei Personalanlässen Finanz- und Rechnungsadministration - Sie kontrollieren und kontieren Kreditkartenbelege und Rechnungen, betreuen die Finanzportale und übernehmen die administrative Abwicklung für die Fördervereinigung (Beiträge, Saldenliste, Jahresabschluss). Büroorganisation & IT-Koordination - Sie organisieren die Büroinfrastruktur inkl. Bestellungen (Material, Geräte, Zubehör), koordinieren einfache IT-Anliegen wie Software-Lizenzen, Mailgruppen und Zugriffsrechte und sorgen für eine einladende Atmosphäre in der Begegnungszone. Sonderaufgaben & Jahresprojekte - Sie unterstützen bei wiederkehrenden Grossprojekten wie der Organisation unserer jährlichen Fachtagung, der Erstellung des Jahresberichts sowie bei unseren Social Media- und Medienauftritten. Ihr Profil Kaufmännische Grundbildung Berufserfahrung in der Administration und Organisation eines Sekretariats Sprachkenntnisse: Deutsch (fliessend), Englisch (in Wort und Schrift) Sehr gute IT-Anwender Kenntnisse (affin mit neuen Programmen) Freundliches, kommunikatives Auftreten, schnelle Auffassungsgabe, vernetztes Denke, Dienstleitungsorientiert Hohe Teamfähigkeit, Integration in bestehendes Team Wir erforschen und gestalten resiliente, nachhaltige und digitale Supply Chains in einem zunehmend komplexen und volatilen Umfeld. Im Zentrum stehen integrierte Produktions-, Logistik- und Innovationssysteme, die ökologische, ökonomische und soziale Zielsetzungen vereinen. Unsere Arbeiten verbinden analytische Modelle, datengetriebene Methoden und simulationsbasierte Ansätze mit realen Fallstudien und Pilotprojekten. Dabei adressieren wir Risiken, Regulierung und Governance ebenso wie technologische und organisatorische Innovationen. Ein besonderer Fokus liegt auf kooperativen, zirkulären und plattformbasierten Geschäftsmodellen. Neue Technologien wie KI, digitale Zwillinge und Industrial Data Spaces werden systematisch in Planung, Steuerung und Entscheidungsfindung integriert. Gleichzeitig rücken wir den Menschen und vertrauenswürdige, rechtskonforme KI in den Mittelpunkt hybrider Intelligenzsysteme. In enger Zusammenarbeit mit Unternehmen, öffentlichen Akteuren und internationalen Partnern entwickeln wir zukunftsfähige Lösungen für globale Supply Chains. Wir freuen uns auf Ihre Online-Bewerbung gerne unter Angabe der Stellen-ID 2833 Hier bewerben Inspirierendes Arbeitsumfeld Weiterbildung Netzwerk Familie & Beruf Chancengleichheit Fit und Gesund Inspirierendes Arbeitsumfeld An der HSG als führende Wirtschaftsuniversität Europas agieren wir in einem unternehmerisch denkenden Umfeld und Sie treffen auf hochqualifizierte, ambitionierte Expert*innen regional und international. Beispielsweise profitieren Sie von einer modernen IT-Infrastruktur und in unserer Bibliothek via HSGswisscovery von einem schweizweiten Zugang zum wissenschaftlichen Informationsbestand. Weiterbildung Wir unterstützen interne und externe Weiterbildungsmöglichkeiten. Unser internes Weiterbildungsprogramm bietet Ihnen praxisnahe, engagierte und didaktisch ausgereifte Wissensvermittlung in Form von Seminaren, E-Learnings, Coachings und kollegialer Beratung. Aufgabenspezifische externe Weiterbildungen unterstützen wir finanziell und zeitlich. Netzwerk Wir fördern unsere Kultur der bereichsübergreifenden Zusammenarbeit und schaffen Raum für das Knüpfen wertvoller Beziehungen – auch zu externen Partner*innen. Regelmässiger Austausch und interne Veranstaltungen helfen diese Beziehung zu festigen und langanhaltend zu gestalten. Familie & Beruf Wir stellen unseren Mitarbeitenden flexible Arbeitszeitmodelle mit variabler Wochenstundenanzahl zur Verfügung. Als familienfreundliche Arbeitgeberin bieten wir Teilzeitanstellungen an, 16 Wochen Mutterschaftsurlaub und eine subventionierte Kinderkrippe sowie Betreuungsangebote in den Ferien. Chancengleichheit Die Universität ermöglicht allen Beschäftigten und Studierenden die gleichen Chancen. Das betrifft das Studium, die Arbeit genauso wie die akademische Karriere, die Besetzung universitärer Leitungsfunktionen oder die Vereinbarkeit von Studium, Beruf und privatem Engagement. Hierfür engagieren wir uns mit diversen Massnahmen in den Bereichen Lehre, Forschung, Verwaltung und Rektorat. Fit und Gesund Wir unterstützen Sie, fit und gesund zu bleiben. Neben unserem vielseitigen, grösstenteils kostenfreien Unisportangebot und Aktionswochen zum betrieblichen Gesundheitsmanagement bieten wir Ihnen Früchte am Arbeitsplatz. In unserer Mensa finden Sie eine breite Auswahl an frisch zubereiteten Gerichten – von vegetarischen Speisen bis hin zu Fischgerichten – zu vergünstigten Preisen. Weitere Informationen zum Arbeiten an der HSG finden Sie hier. Für Fragen zur Stelle Prof. Dr. Julia Arlinghaus Direktorin Supply Chain Management Der Mensch ist der entscheidende Erfolgsfaktor. Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Ludwig Häberle Vizedirektor Ich würde mich sehr freuen, Sie bald an der Universi-tät St.Gallen willkommen zu heissen. Ihre offenen Fragen beantworte ich Ihnen jederzeit gerne. Ihr Arbeitsort Die HSG «Ein Ort, der Wissen schafft» - Als eine der führenden Wirtschaftsuniversitäten Europas engagiert sich die Universität St.Gallen (HSG) in der Ausbildung von über 10'000 Studierenden und bietet als eine der grössten Arbeitgeberinnen der Region rund 3'800 Mitarbeitenden ein attraktives und innovatives Umfeld in Forschung, Lehre, Weiterbildung und Verwaltung.» Weitere Stellen PhD Position in Cybersecurity and Applied Cryptography (m/f/d) Institute of Computer Science 80-100% Wissenschaftliche Hilfskraft / Forschungsassistenz bei Prof. em. Dr. Thomas Bieger (m/w/d) Institut für Systemisches Management und Public Governance 50-80%, 10-50% Student Assistant - Custom Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) 10-50% Teilen share-solid Teilen Hier bewerben"
    },
    "https://jobs.unisg.ch/offene-stellen/phd-candidate-research-associate-in-asset-management-m-f-d/be395e1c-08e7-40e1-b442-52821ec6cdf3": {
      "title": "PhD candidate / Research Associate in Asset Management (m/f/d)",
      "description": "HSG: PhD candidate / Research Associate in Asset Management (m/f/d) Accounting Controlling & Auditing PhD candidate / Research Associate in Asset Management (m/f/d) PhD candidate / Research Associate in Asset Management (m/f/d) Workload 75 %\n            \n            \n                (limited from 01.12.2026 or as agreed) Your tasks Independent research activities in a young, dynamic, and international team Support in executive education on asset management Support of the Chair of Corporate Finance Participation at international conferences and workshops Collaborative work with a high degree of personal responsibility Your profile High personal motivation and responsible work ethics Keen interest in learning how to work scientifically as a base for an academic or professional career Excellent marks in your diploma, licentiate, or master studies in the finance or corporate finance classes Excellent knowledge of asset management and good knowledge of corporate finance Fluent in German and strong English spoken and written communication skills Adept at communicating with finance professionals The Chair of Prof. Dr. Marc Arnold is primarily active in corporate finance and asset management. Our core competences are teaching, research, and executive education. The PhD-position focuses on asset management topics. We offer you the possibility to work in a dynamic and challenging research environment and present your work at international conferences. The focus of your work is on the collaboration in research projects and executive education in asset management. We value target oriented and constructive team players that are able to collaborate with both acedemics and practitioners. Please send us your application by November, 15th. We are looking forward to your online-application stating the job ID apply here Inspirational Work Environment Executive Education Network Family & Career Equal Opportunities Fit and Healthy Inspirational Work Environment At the HSG, as Europe's leading business university, we operate in an entrepreneurial environment where you will meet highly qualified, ambitious experts - both regionally and internationally. For example, you benefit from a modern IT infrastructure and, in our library via HSGswisscovery, from nationwide access to the wealth of scientific information available. Executive Education We support internal and external executive education opportunities. Our internal executive education programme offers you a practical, dedicated and didactically mature transfer of knowledge in the form of seminars, e-learning, coaching and collegial advice. We support task-specific external training and executive education financially as well as with regard to the time required. Network We promote our culture of cross-functional collaboration and create space for forging valuable relationships - also with external partners. Regular exchanges and internal events help to strengthen these relationships and make them long-lasting. Family & Career We provide our employees with flexible work time models with a variable number of hours per week. As a family-friendly employer, we offer part-time positions, 16 weeks of maternity leave and a subsidised crèche, as well as support with childcare during the vacations. Equal Opportunities The University enables equal opportunities for all employees and students. This applies to degree courses and work, as well as academic careers, university management positions and the reconciliation of studies, work and private commitments. We are committed to this with various measures in the areas of teaching, research, administration and the Presidency. Fit and Healthy We help you stay fit and healthy. In addition to our diverse range of sports activities at the university, most of which are free of charge, and campaign weeks for corporate health management, we also offer you fruit in the workplace. In our canteen you will find a wide selection of freshly prepared meals - from vegetarian to fish dishes - at discounted prices. Further information on working at the HSG can be found here. For job-related questions Prof. Dr. Marc Arnold Institutsdirektor We offer an active and internationally oriented research environment. Carolina Näf Personal Assistant We are looking forward to receive your application! Your place of work University of St.Gallen «A place where knowledge is created» - As one of Europe's leading universities of economics and business administration, the University of St.Gallen (HSG), Switzerland, is committed to the education of over 10'000 students. The HSG is one of the largest employers in the region and provides an attractive and innovative environment for more than 3'800 researchers, educators and professional staff. Other Jobs PhD Position in Cybersecurity and Applied Cryptography (m/f/d) Institute of Computer Science 80-100% Wissenschaftliche Hilfskraft / Forschungsassistenz bei Prof. em. Dr. Thomas Bieger (m/w/d) Institut für Systemisches Management und Public Governance 50-80%, 10-50% Student Assistant - Custom Programmes ES HSG (m/w/d) Executive School of Management, Technology and Law (ES HSG) 10-50% Share share-solid Share apply here"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409856": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in Macroeconomics (100%)School of Economics and Political Science",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in Macroeconomics (100%) School of Economics and Political Science «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in Macroeconomics (100%) The University of St.Gallen and its School of Economics and Political Science are inviting applications for an Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in the field of macroeconomics. Candidates with a focus in applied macroeconomics are particularly encouraged to apply. Candidates should have (or aim to establish) a promising record of internationally recognized research and show commitment to teaching excellence. Ideal candidates have an emerging track record of internationally recognized research in leading general interest or field journals. Successful candidates will teach in our Economics or International Affairs programmes. Candidates should have a commitment to academic leadership and citizenship, including contributions to public discourse and outreach activities. Experience in the acquisition of third-party funding is a plus. The appointment is for 6 years, with an intermediate evaluation after 3 years. Based on the tenure track process, successful candidates can be promoted to a tenured Associate Professor position. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position per August 1st, 2027, or by mutual agreement. Interviews will take place online at the European Job Market for Economists (EJME). Short-listed candidates will then be invited to present their research and have an interview with the hiring committee in St. Gallen in January 2027. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Winfried Koeniger, Chair of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching and research statement, list of research papers including publications, identification of the job-market paper, and two reference letters. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr Manuel Ammann online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by October 31 st , 2026. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 3 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409857": {
      "title": "Selectus",
      "description": "Selectus - University of St.Gallen Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen More English Deutsch Ordentliche Professur für Gesellschaftsrecht (100%) Law School «Ein Ort der Wissen schafft» – Als führende Wirtschaftsuniversität setzen wir in Forschung und Lehre weltweit Massstäbe, indem wir integratives Denken, verantwortungsvolles Handeln und unternehmerischen Innovationsgeist in Wirtschaft und Gesellschaft fördern. Ordentliche Professur für Gesellschaftsrecht (100%) An der Rechtswissenschaftlichen Abteilung (Law School) der Universität St.Gallen ist auf den 1. Februar 2028 oder nach Vereinbarung eine Ordentliche Professur für Gesellschaftsrecht zu besetzen. Besetzt werden kann die Stelle mit einem Beschäftigungsgrad von 100%, oder nach Vereinbarung mit 75%. Voraussetzung für den Stellenantritt ist eine Habilitation oder eine habilitationsäquivalente Leistung mit Schwerpunkt im Gesellschaftsrecht. Sie verfügen zudem über einen qualitativ hochwertigen Forschungsausweis, der das Gesellschaftsrecht in seiner ganzen Breite abdeckt – idealerweise mit Schwerpunkt im schweizerischen Recht, mindestens aber mit klarem Bezug dazu. Sie sind eine unternehmerische Persönlichkeit und haben Freude an kollaborativer Forschung sowie an interdisziplinärer Zusammenarbeit, insbesondere mit Kolleginnen und Kollegen der School of Management. Sie bringen Lehrerfahrung im Gesellschaftsrecht mit exzellenten Evaluationen mit und können sowohl auf Deutsch als auch auf Englisch unterrichten. In Ihrer künftigen Rolle beteiligen Sie sich massgeblich an den Kernveranstaltungen der Law School in diesem wichtigen Fachbereich bzw. übernehmen dafür die Verantwortung. Von Vorteil ist Interesse und Erfahrung in der Weiterbildung. Sie leisten einen sichtbaren Beitrag zu nationalen und internationalen wissenschaftlichen Debatten im Gesellschaftsrecht, unter anderem durch die Organisation von und Teilnahme an einschlägigen Tagungen, und bringen sich aktiv in die nationale öffentliche Debatte des Fachbereichs ein. Sie engagieren sich zudem in der akademischen Selbstverwaltung und universitären Gremienarbeit. Ein starkes Netzwerk in der Praxis sowie nachgewiesene Erfolge bei der kompetitiven Einwerbung von Drittmitteln runden Ihr Profil ab. Die Universität St.Gallen setzt sich für eine inklusive Arbeitskultur und für Diversität ein. Wir bieten einen Dual-Career und Welcome Service für unsere neuberufenen Professorinnen und Professoren (und deren Familien) an. Nähere Auskünfte zum Profil erteilen Prof. Dr. Peter Hettich (Dean Law School, peter.hettich@unisg.ch ) oder Faculty Affairs ( berufungen@unisg.ch ). Interessentinnen und Interessenten richten ihre Bewerbung bitte mit den üblichen Unterlagen (Anschreiben, CV, Publikationsliste, Nachweise der didaktischen Eignung [z. B. Evaluationen], Lehr- und Forschungsprofil [max. je 1 A4-Seite]) in elektronischer Form bis spätestens 20. November 2026 online über https://www.unisg.ch/professorships an den Rektor der Universität St.Gallen, Professor Dr. Manuel Ammann. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 5 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409858": {
      "title": "Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise SystemsSchool of Management",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise Systems School of Management «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise Systems The University of St.Gallen and its School of Management are inviting applications for a Full Professorship / Associate Professorship (Open Rank) in Data Management and Enterprise Systems. The triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA) university offers a stimulating and well-equipped research environment with a large network ranging from start-ups to multinational companies, providing excellent opportunities for research and industry collaboration. The new professorship will become part of the School of Management and strengthen the University's interdisciplinary activities at the interface of management, information systems, data science and computer science. We are seeking a colleague with internationally recognised expertise in one or more of the fields of Data Management, Enterprise Systems, Enterprise Architecture, or related areas. The ideal candidate has an internationally recognised track record of leading research in Information Systems, reflected in multiple publications in leading international journals (FT50), a strong pipeline of promising research projects, a strong international academic network, close ties with industry, and excellent teaching skills at all levels, including Executive Education. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the School's teaching portfolio in core areas of Information Systems such as Data Management. According to our claim \"From insight to impact\", the future colleague should convey scientific knowledge to students and have a significant impact on theory and practice. Depending on qualifications, the appointment will be made at the level of Full Professor or Associate Professor. Candidates for a Full Professorship are expected to demonstrate internationally leading scholarly achievements, sustained success in attracting competitive external research funding, academic leadership, and a broad contribution to the development of their field. The successful candidate is expected to play a key role in strengthening interdisciplinary collaboration between the School of Management and other schools, particularly the School of Computer Science. The position includes developing collaborative research initiatives, contributing to interdisciplinary teaching, strengthening partnerships with industry, attracting competitive external research funding (e.g. SNF, Innosuisse, ERC, EU or industry collaborations), and contributing actively to the academic community and the governance of the University. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position as of 1 August 2027 or by mutual agreement. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Björn Ambos, Dean of the School of  Management and Chairman of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter specifying the academic rank for which the applicant wishes to be considered, a curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements (max. one page each), a list of publications, teaching evaluations, two publications that best represent the applicant's fit to the advertised position, and contact information for two professional references whom we may contact should the applicant be shortlisted for the position. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr  Manuel Ammann, online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by 15 November 2026. Research talks are expected to take place on 18 January 2027. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 6 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409861": {
      "title": "Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship Technology and Information ManagementSchool of Management",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship Technology and Information Management School of Management «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship with Tenure Track (Open Rank) in Technology and Innovation Management The University of St.Gallen and its School of Management are inviting applications for an Associate Professorship / Assistant Professorship with Tenure Track (Open Rank) in Technology and Innovation Management. The triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA) university offers a stimulating and well-equipped research environment with a large network ranging from start-ups, small businesses to large firms to engage in research. The new professorship in the School of Management will become part of our dynamic faculty and will be invited to join the Institute of Technology Management (ITEM-HSG) and the Global Center for Entrepreneurship and Innovation. We are seeking a colleague with proven expertise in one or more of the key domains of Technology and Innovation Management, including Global R&D, Innovation Strategy, Digital Innovation, Open Innovation, AI-driven Innovation, Technology Strategy, or related fields. Depending on qualifications, the appointment will be made at the level of Associate Professor or Assistant Professor with Tenure Track. The ideal candidate for the Associate Professorship has an internationally recognised and leading track record in research in leading journals in the field of Technology and Innovation Management, reflected in publications in top journals (e.g. FT50), a strong pipeline of promising research projects, a strong international academic network, ties with industry, and excellent teaching skills at all levels, including Executive Education. According to our claim \"From insight to impact\", the future colleague should convey scientific knowledge to students and have a significant impact on theory and practice. The successful candidate will also attract competitive external research funding (e.g. SNF, Innosuisse, ERC or industry collaborations), contribute actively to the academic community and governance of the University, and strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration across the School of Management and related technology-oriented disciplines. Associate Professors at the University of St.Gallen are provided with a budget to hire a doctoral student. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position as of 1 August 2027 or by mutual agreement. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Björn Ambos, Dean of the School of Management and Chairman of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements (max. one page each), list of publications, teaching evaluations, two publications or working papers that best represent the applicant's current research, and contact information for two professional references that we may contact if shortlisted for the position. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr Manuel Ammann, online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by 15 November 2026. Research talks are expected to take place on 20 January 2027. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 7 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    },
    "https://facultyrecruiting.unisg.ch/positiondetails/28409860": {
      "title": "Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in EntrepreneurshipSchool of Management",
      "description": "Selectus - Home Skip to main content Log out University of St.Gallen English Deutsch Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in Entrepreneurship School of Management «A place where knowledge is created» – As a leading business university we set global standards for research and teaching by promoting integrative thought, responsible action and an entrepreneurial spirit of innovation in business and society. Assistant Professorship (Tenure Track) in Entrepreneurship The University of St.Gallen and its School of Management are inviting applications for an Assistant Professorship with Tenure Track in Entrepreneurship, including SME or Family Business. The triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA) university offers a stimulating and well-equipped research environment with a large network ranging from start-ups, small businesses and family firms to large corporations, providing outstanding opportunities for research and collaboration. The new professorship in the School of Management will be invited to become part of the Swiss Research Institute of Small Business and Entrepreneurship (KMU-HSG). We are seeking an outstanding early-career scholar with a clear research focus in Entrepreneurship, or closely related fields such as Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) or Family Business. The successful candidate should demonstrate strong potential for publishing in leading international journals (e.g., FT50), an ambitious and internationally visible research agenda, and the ability to build a strong academic network. The successful candidate is expected to conduct internationally recognised research, actively acquire competitive external research funding (in particular SNF, Innosuisse, ERC), and contribute to the further development of the research profile of the KMU-HSG, the School of Management, and the University of St.Gallen overall. Applicants should therefore demonstrate outstanding academic potential and the ability to develop into an internationally recognized scholar. The position involves teaching at Bachelor and Master levels in English. The successful candidate will contribute to the School's teaching portfolio in areas such as Entrepreneurship, Small Business Management, Family Business, and related subjects. We are looking for candidates with excellent teaching skills who are committed to developing innovative teaching formats and inspiring students at all levels. The University of St.Gallen is committed to promoting equal opportunities and an inclusive working culture. We explicitly encourage women and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We offer dual-career and welcome services for newly appointed faculty (and their families). We seek to fill the position as of 1 August 2027 or by mutual agreement. For further information, please contact Professor Dr Björn Ambos, Dean of the School of Management and Chairman of the Appointment Committee ( facultyposition@unisg.ch ). The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae including list of publications, research and teaching statement (each max. one page), teaching evaluations, two research papers that best represent the applicant's current research and contact information for two academic references. Candidates should submit their application to the President of the University of St.Gallen, Professor Dr Manuel Ammann, online via www.unisg.ch/professorships at the latest by 15 November 2026. Research talks are expected to take place on 21 January 2027. Apply online Go to top © 2026 St.Gallen University | Disclaimer | \n\t12 October 2026 ( 8 People are online) Selectus 5.6.5 × Unsaved form data Attention! You have not saved this form yet. By clicking Do not save data you will exit the form without saving. Changes you made on this page will be lost By clicking Back to form you will get back to the form where you can save it. Back to form Do not save data"
    }
  },
